.build/
.swiftpm/
xcuserdata/
.DS_Store
# The whole generated project, not just the parts Xcode writes into it.
#
# It used to be committed, with only project.pbxproj tracked and the workspace
# and xcuserdata ignored beneath it, so the repo would open without XcodeGen
# installed. That made project.yml and the project two sources of truth for the
# same thing: change the spec, forget to regenerate, and the build uses the
# stale one without complaining. Xcode Cloud now regenerates it on every build
# via ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh, which removed the only argument for keeping
# it. Run `xcodegen generate` after cloning.
#
# This supersedes the two narrower rules that lived here, and PeachMinimal's,
# all of which this covers.
*.xcodeproj/
# Archives have been written into .build/ so far, which covered these by
# accident rather than by intent. An xcarchive is a signed copy of the whole
# app and has no business in the history.
*.xcarchive
DerivedData/
# Where ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh unpacks its pinned XcodeGen. Written into
# the repo root because that is the only writable place it can rely on.
.ci-tools/
